/*
 * Declares the EnumType class.
 *
 * An enumeration type is a proxy over another type, but restraining a subset of
 * values when constructed. Inner type is always const, to make it mutable, it
 * must be extracted from the enumeration by a cast. Movable types cannot
 * describe enumeration values.
 *
 * <hr>
 *
 * @Package: ymirc
 * @Module: ymirc::semantic::generator::type::custom::enum_
 * @File: ymirc/semantic/generator/type/custom/enum_.yr
 * @Author(s):
 *   - Emile Cadorel <ecadorel@gmail.com>
 *
 * @Created (YYYY-MM-DD): 2021-11-20
